# Halogen settings for this machine. Copied once to /srv/configs/halogen.env, then it is yours.
# After an update, sudo halogenctl options --new lists options your file doesn't mention yet.
#
# Uncomment a line and set its value, then run: sudo halogenctl restart
# Check what is in effect with: sudo halogenctl config
# Only the options listed here are used. Anything else is ignored and logged.
# Locked settings are in /usr/share/halogen/locked.env.
# The full reference is docs/FLAGS.md in Halogen's repository.

## Model and tokenizer

# How many tokens the draft head proposes in a row for a greedy request (the head drafts, the model verifies... Default: unset
#HALOGEN_MTP_DEPTH=

# How sure the draft head must be to keep extending its chain, for a greedy request. Default: 0.90
#HALOGEN_MTP_GATE_P=

# How many tokens the draft head may propose in a row for a sampled request (temperature above 0) that runs... Default: 7
#HALOGEN_SAMPLED_DEPTH=

# When a sampled request's draft chain may grow, as t1,t2. Default: 0.95,0.98
#HALOGEN_SAMPLED_GATE=

# The model id listed at /v1/models, reported at /health, and echoed in every completion. Default: halogen-qwen3.8-flash-next
#HALOGEN_MODEL_ID=

# The end-of-turn guard (0.13.4, issue #84). Default: (unset: on); 0 = off
#HALOGEN_EOS_GUARD=

# The end-of-turn guard in the answer (0.18.15, issue #89. Default: (unset: on); 0 = off
#HALOGEN_ANSWER_GUARD=

## Networking

# Which requests print a line on the console. Default: quiet
#HALOGEN_ACCESS_LOG=

## Request policy

# Largest max_tokens a request may ask for. Default: 65536
#HALOGEN_MAX_TOKENS_CAP=

# Seconds an idle keep-alive connection is held open before the server closes it. Default: 300
#HALOGEN_KEEPALIVE_TIMEOUT=

# On a streaming response, an SSE comment line (. Default: 10
#HALOGEN_SSE_KEEPALIVE_S=

# Seconds a reply is paused when its client disconnects in the middle of it, waiting for the same request to... Default: 20
#HALOGEN_RETRY_GRACE_S=

# Seconds a queued request waits before 503 engine_busy. Default: 3600
#HALOGEN_QUEUE_TIMEOUT=

# The token budget a request gets when it sends none. Default: (unset: 8192 on chat and responses, 128 on completions)
#HALOGEN_MAX_TOKENS_DEFAULT=

# The sampling temperature for a request that sends none, 0 to 2. Default: (unset: greedy)
#HALOGEN_TEMPERATURE=

# top_p for a request that sends none, 0 to 1. Default: (unset: no nucleus filter)
#HALOGEN_TOP_P=

# top_k for a request that sends none. Default: (unset: no top-k filter)
#HALOGEN_TOP_K=

# min_p for a request that sends none, 0 to 1. Default: (unset: off)
#HALOGEN_MIN_P=

# presence_penalty for a request that sends none, -2 to 2. Default: (unset: 0)
#HALOGEN_PRESENCE_PENALTY=

# frequency_penalty for a request that sends none, -2 to 2. Default: (unset: 0)
#HALOGEN_FREQUENCY_PENALTY=

# The repetition penalty for a sampled request that sends none (0.15.1). Default: (unset: 1, off)
#HALOGEN_REPETITION_PENALTY=

# The reasoning effort for a request that names none. Default: (unset: the chat template's own xhigh)
#HALOGEN_REASONING_EFFORT=

# Whether a request that does not say renders the thinking block. Default: (unset: the chat template's own default, thinking on)
#HALOGEN_ENABLE_THINKING=

# The thinking budget for a request that sends none (0.8.1, issue #56). Default: (unset: no budget)
#HALOGEN_MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=

# The text the server writes before </think> when it closes the think block itself. Default: (unset: the model's own budget sentence); set and empty = </think> alone
#HALOGEN_THINKING_BUDGET_MESSAGE=

# The answer room (0.11.0). Default: (unset: max(1024, 15% of the request's max_tokens)); 0 = off
#HALOGEN_THINKING_ANSWER_ROOM=

# Which drafter a request that names none gets. Default: 1
#HALOGEN_DRAFTER_DEFAULT=

# How many requests generating at once still speculate together (since 0.18.11). Default: 4; 0 = off
#HALOGEN_SPEC_GROUP=

# Prompt lookup beside the MTP head, as N,K. Default: 3,3
#HALOGEN_PLD=

# The MTP head's adaptive policy, as W,floor,R. Default: 32,0.35,64
#HALOGEN_SPEC_ADAPT=

# Structured output: whether a response_format of json_schema / json_object (text.format on /v1/responses)... Default: 1
#HALOGEN_GRAMMAR=

# Strict tool schemas (since 0.18.2). Default: 1
#HALOGEN_STRICT_TOOLS=

# How a chat-template marker written inside your own text is read (since 0.18.2). Default: text
#HALOGEN_CLIENT_MARKERS=

## Images

# Path to the vision sidecar, or 1 to look for it beside the checkpoint. Default: (unset: images are refused)
#HALOGEN_VISION_TOWER=

# The most pixels an image is given before it is downscaled to fit, preserving aspect ratio. Default: 3686400 (2560x1440)
#HALOGEN_VISION_MAX_PIXELS=

## Context and concurrency

# Conversations generating at once. Default: 4
#HALOGEN_KV_SLOTS=

# Attention positions resident across all conversations. Default: 2 x HALOGEN_CTX, capped at 1,048,576 (the cap applies to the default only)
HALOGEN_KV_POOL_POSITIONS=262144

# Whether the server measures the device budget at startup and lowers HALOGEN_KV_POOL_POSITIONS when the... Default: 1
#HALOGEN_KV_POOL_FIT=

# When the server had to lower a request's max_tokens to the room its conversation had left in the KV pool,... Default: 2
#HALOGEN_POOL_GROW=

# NUMERIC, opt-in. 1 keeps the attention cache (its keys and values) in 8 bits instead of 16, which nearly... Default: unset (off)
#HALOGEN_KV8=

# The kernel's out-of-memory score adjustment the server's processes start with. Default: 500; 0 leaves it
#HALOGEN_OOM_SCORE_ADJ=

# How much system RAM the server leaves free, on top of the weights, when it sizes the KV pool at startup. Default: 20
#HALOGEN_HOST_RESERVE_GIB=

# The most context ONE request may use, the model's full native context, by default. Default: 262144
#HALOGEN_CTX=

# How a prompt is read in when other conversations are already generating. Default: 0 (the engine's own prefill chunk)
#HALOGEN_ADMIT_CHUNK=

# How many generation steps the conversations already generating get between two pieces of a prompt being... Default: 1
#HALOGEN_ADMIT_TICKS=

# Keeps replies that are already streaming moving while another request's prompt is read in. Default: 500; 0 = off
#HALOGEN_ADMIT_SPLICE_MS=

# Which streaming replies HALOGEN_ADMIT_SPLICE_MS keeps moving. Default: all
#HALOGEN_ADMIT_SPLICE_FOR=

# Lets a short request that arrives while another request's long prompt is being read start right away... Default: 1; 0 = off
#HALOGEN_ADMIT_NEST=

# The largest request, in tokens not already cached, that HALOGEN_ADMIT_NEST starts during another's read. Default: 1024
#HALOGEN_ADMIT_NEST_MAX=

# How many prompt-cache entries the server keeps. Default: 24
#HALOGEN_CACHE_ENTRIES=

# Which prompt-cache entry goes first when the cache holds HALOGEN_CACHE_ENTRIES entries. Default: 2
#HALOGEN_CACHE_EVICT=

# For Claude Code and Codex, which send the same project instructions at the start of every new thread (the... Default: 1; 0 = off
#HALOGEN_CACHE_LEAD=

# How many branches of one conversation the prompt cache keeps resume points for. Default: 2
#HALOGEN_CACHE_BRANCHES=

# Whether the prompt cache also saves its place at the START of the last user message. Default: 1; 0 = off
#HALOGEN_CACHE_SNAP3=

# Whether the server keeps the end-of-request entry (0.11.3). Default: 1; 0 = off
#HALOGEN_CACHE_FULL=

# Largest single prefill call. Default: 32768
#HALOGEN_MAX_TOK=

# The prompt cache keeps the conversation's attention state where it already is and saves only the small... Default: 1
#HALOGEN_CACHE_INPLACE=

# How the prompt cache copies a conversation's state to and from host memory. Default: 2
#HALOGEN_CACHE_STAGE=

# Contexts past the native 262,144, up to 1,048,576. Default: (unset)
#HALOGEN_ROPE_YARN=

# The model's sparse-attention budget. Default: (unset) = 2048
#HALOGEN_INDEXER_BUDGET=

## Speed levers

# Reuse a session's shared prefix instead of re-reading it. Default: 2 (resume anywhere)
#HALOGEN_PROMPT_CACHE=

# How many tokens the engine prefills per call. Default: 32768
#HALOGEN_PREFILL_CHUNK=

# NUMERIC, opt-in preview. 1 retains each message at or above HALOGEN_COMPOSABLE_CONTEXT_FLOOR as it is... Default: 0 (off)
#HALOGEN_COMPOSABLE_CONTEXT=

# The smallest message composable context retains and reuses. Default: 2048 (tokens)
#HALOGEN_COMPOSABLE_CONTEXT_FLOOR=

# The host-memory budget of the retained messages, least recently used out. Default: 4294967296 (4 GiB)
#HALOGEN_COMPOSABLE_CONTEXT_BYTES=

# How many rows of the model's lookup table are read at once when a prompt needs rows that are not in the... Default: 64
#HALOGEN_NGRAM_GATHER_THREADS=

# 1 keeps the default checkpoint's trunk weights unpacked in memory for the server's life, so prefill does... Default: 0 (off)
#HALOGEN_PREFILL_KEEP_TRUNK=

## Request records

# Which text the records keep. Default: none on halOS (counts only; recording is off until: sudo halogenctl records on)
#HALOGEN_RECORD_TEXT=

# The size cap of the records directory, in GiB, over everything in it. Default: 2
#HALOGEN_RECORD_GIB=

# How many days of records to keep. Default: 90
#HALOGEN_RECORD_DAYS=

## Sessions: keep, fork and join

# Let a client keep a conversation's state under a name and start later requests from it. Default: 1 (on)
#HALOGEN_FORK=

# The most names kept at once. Default: 8
#HALOGEN_FORK_HANDLES=

# A name not used for this many seconds is released. Default: 600
#HALOGEN_FORK_TTL_S=

# The most host memory kept states may hold, in GiB (a named state about 0.2 GiB). Default: 2
#HALOGEN_FORK_GIB=

# claude-code: with HALOGEN_FORK=1, keep each Claude Code thread's state (the main conversation and each... Default: (unset) = off
#HALOGEN_FORK_MAP=

## Troubleshooting

# A request cancelled while its prompt is still being read (its client hung up, or the front end cancelled... Default: 1 (on)
#HALOGEN_PREFILL_CANCEL=

# For a host whose GPU firmware predates 2026 (MEC firmware below 0x22. Default: (unset: follows the GPU firmware); 1 = on, 0 = off
#HALOGEN_QSA_FORCE_SEL=

# For a host with more than one AMD GPU, such as a Strix Halo with an AMD eGPU. Default: (unset: the Strix Halo GPU); auto = unset
#HALOGEN_GPU_DEVICE=

# Whether the server narrates how it is armed at startup, on top of what it is serving. Default: 0 in this image
#HALOGEN_VERBOSE=

# Whether the server says which startup step it is on and how long it has taken. Default: 1 (on)
#HALOGEN_STARTUP_PROGRESS=

# How long the engine may go without answering the container's liveness probe before the container is taken... Default: 180 (seconds); 0 = off
#HALOGEN_ENGINE_WATCHDOG_S=

# How long the watchdog keeps deferring a silent engine because the kernel's memory-compaction counter is... Default: 900 (seconds); 0 = no cap
#HALOGEN_ENGINE_WATCHDOG_DEFER_S=

# How long a stream waits between two tokens before it answers 504. Default: derived: 990 at the defaults; 300 with the watchdog off; 1800 with no deferral cap
#HALOGEN_NEXT_TOKEN_S=

# How long the container waits for the engine to finish loading before giving up. Default: 0 (wait as long as the load takes)
#HALOGEN_ENGINE_WAIT_S=

# 1 locks the weights into RAM (mlock) so the kernel cannot reclaim them (0.13.2). Default: 0 (off)
#HALOGEN_WEIGHTS_LOCK=

# Whether the weights are locked into memory. Default: 1 (on)
#HALOGEN_FLASH_PIN_TRUNK=

# When to warn that the host's free memory is in the wrong SHAPE. Default: 512
#HALOGEN_FRAG_WARN_BLOCKS=

# The same problem measured directly instead of predicted. Default: 1000
#HALOGEN_FRAG_WARN_STALLS=

# 1 prints every device allocation of 64 MB or more as it happens, with its size, a running total and a count. Default: 0
#HALOGEN_DMALLOC_LOG=

## The NPU

# Small models to serve on the Ryzen AI NPU beside the Flash model, comma-separated, on the same port. Default: (unset: no NPU)
HALOGEN_NPU_MODELS=decider-0.8b,qwen3-embedding-0.6b,qwen3-reranker-0.6b,qwen3guard-gen-0.6b,qwen3.5-2b

# /v1/embeddings and /v1/rerank. Default: 1
#HALOGEN_NPU_EMB_BATCH=

# With qwen3guard-stream-0.6b in HALOGEN_NPU_MODELS. Default: 4
#HALOGEN_GUARD_STREAMS=

# The streaming guard's Unsafe probability at which a watched chunk of a reply is flagged (flagged. Default: 0.8
#HALOGEN_GUARD_FLAG=

# How many characters of a watched reply may wait for the streaming guard. Default: 4096
#HALOGEN_GUARD_LAG=

# How long, in seconds, the end of a watched streamed reply waits for the streaming guard's last verdicts... Default: 3
#HALOGEN_GUARD_FINAL_S=

# A preview: a second pair of eyes for an agent, not a security boundary. Default: off
#HALOGEN_AGENT_GUARD=

# With HALOGEN_NPU_MODELS: how many NPU passes may wait on the NPU at once. Default: 64
#HALOGEN_NPU_QUEUE=

# With HALOGEN_NPU_MODELS: a short request to one NPU model (a decision, an embedding, a rerank or a... Default: 1; 0 = off
#HALOGEN_NPU_SPLICE=

# With HALOGEN_NPU_MODELS: if the NPU engine stops while the Flash model serves (it exits on its own when... Default: 3
#HALOGEN_NPU_RESTARTS=

# The NPU engine's models live in host memory that cannot be swapped, and each one takes more as it is used. Default: 4; 0 turns it off
#HALOGEN_NPU_HOST_FLOOR_GIB=
